    {
      "id": "r1huwts",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "2.2.1 Mahadayi (Kalasa-Banduri) Water Dispute"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ox6g9so",
      "content": "The Mahadayi River water dispute is one of the most significant inter-state disputes involving Goa. Goa opposes the diversion of Mahadayi waters to meet drinking water needs of North Karnataka and to fill the Malaprabha reservoir."
    },
    {
      "id": "8e7x0sb",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Dispute is between Goa, Karnataka, and Maharashtra",
        "Mahadayi Water Disputes Tribunal set up in 2010",
        "The tribunal gave its final award in 2018, allowing Karnataka 13.42 TMC of water",
        "Goa has been opposing the diversion due to impact on ecology and biodiversity",
        "The river is critical for Goa's drinking water supply and wildlife"
      ]
    },
