      "content": "2.4 Western Ghats and Forests"
    },
    {
      "id": "nw6pefh",
      "type": "image",
      "imageId": "abeif3o",
      "src": "/books/Guide/Goa SI/images/image_abeif3o.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2eou76t",
      "content": "<img></img>The eastern part of Goa is covered by the Western Ghats, a UNESCO World Heritage Site and one of the world's eight biodiversity hotspots. The forests provide critical ecosystem services and are home to rare flora and fauna."
    },
    {
      "id": "d9t8id0",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Western Ghats cover approximately 56% of Goa's eastern territory",
        "Bhagwan Mahavir National Park (107 sq.km) — only national park in Goa",
        "Mollem National Park is located within Bhagwan Mahavir NP",
        "Cotigao Wildlife Sanctuary (105 sq.km) — second largest in Goa",
        "Bondla Wildlife Sanctuary — smallest; known as 'Goa's mini zoo'",
        "Netravali Wildlife Sanctuary — known as 'Land of Butterflies'",
        "Madei Wildlife Sanctuary — habitat of the Malabar Giant Squirrel"
      ]
    },
